WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.650 --> 00:00:06.160
There's a story floating around about Elizabeth
Warren that has her taking a lot of heat from

00:00:06.160 --> 00:00:12.900
people on the left because she made one point
$9 million over 30 years doing legal consulting

00:00:12.900 --> 00:00:15.669
work for a number of different corporations.

00:00:15.669 --> 00:00:17.810
Now let me, I don't even know.

00:00:17.810 --> 00:00:19.640
I, I don't even know why I do this.

00:00:19.640 --> 00:00:22.500
I know I'm going to get crushed, but I'll
do the normal disclaimers.

00:00:22.500 --> 00:00:24.550
I'm not endorsing Elizabeth Warren.

00:00:24.550 --> 00:00:30.240
I'm not defending Elizabeth Warren's particular
work in any of the cases we're going to discuss.

00:00:30.240 --> 00:00:33.770
But what I am here to tell you is I think
that some of the critiques around this are

00:00:33.770 --> 00:00:35.790
a little bit misplaced.

00:00:35.790 --> 00:00:42.140
Some people are saying that this Warren thing
is a story of misogyny, that Elizabeth Warren

00:00:42.140 --> 00:00:47.920
is being slammed for making one point $9 million
over 30 years.

00:00:47.920 --> 00:00:52.550
Whereas you have people like Michael Bloomberg
spending 30 million on his own campaign and

00:00:52.550 --> 00:00:53.640
nobody questions it.

00:00:53.640 --> 00:00:55.440
Nobody questions bayzos his income, whatever.

00:00:55.440 --> 00:01:00.210
That that's, there's a an identity politics
thing that's being said about this.

00:01:00.210 --> 00:01:05.180
There are others who are saying this is really
about corporate cronyism, centrists status

00:01:05.180 --> 00:01:11.210
quo politics and Elizabeth Warren not as a
progressive but rather as a tool of the centrist

00:01:11.210 --> 00:01:13.180
corporate establishment.

00:01:13.180 --> 00:01:17.200
So once again, disclosure, this is not an
endorsement of Elizabeth Warren.

00:01:17.200 --> 00:01:22.010
This is a warning that we should pick our
battles and pick battles that make sense,

00:01:22.010 --> 00:01:25.130
particularly within the framework of the democratic
primary.

00:01:25.130 --> 00:01:26.680
So let's go through the facts.

00:01:26.680 --> 00:01:33.700
The report is that Elizabeth Warren put out
a detailed compensation list, partially because

00:01:33.700 --> 00:01:37.640
of pressure from the Pete Buddha judge campaign
and it was revealed that she worked for about

00:01:37.640 --> 00:01:39.520
30 years as a legal consultant.

00:01:39.520 --> 00:01:44.799
There were cases that she worked on as a consultant
while she was teaching law, mostly at Harvard

00:01:44.799 --> 00:01:46.760
and at the university of Pennsylvania.

00:01:46.760 --> 00:01:49.000
Now Elizabeth Warren is an expert in bankruptcy.

00:01:49.000 --> 00:01:52.220
A lot of the cases related to bankruptcy make
sense.

00:01:52.220 --> 00:01:57.020
And in total it was one point $9 million in
income over 30 years.

00:01:57.020 --> 00:02:00.850
So number one, this is about $63,000 a year.

00:02:00.850 --> 00:02:05.760
Now, there's no question that Elizabeth Warren
is hugely privileged.

00:02:05.760 --> 00:02:09.519
We knew that back when she ran for Senate
and I interviewed her in person.

00:02:09.519 --> 00:02:13.599
I said, you know, you have rhetoric that is
one thing, and at the same time you are very

00:02:13.599 --> 00:02:14.599
wealthy yourself.

00:02:14.599 --> 00:02:17.379
She's, her net worth is known to be around
10 to $12 million.

00:02:17.379 --> 00:02:20.329
Now I think it was more in the single digits
then.

00:02:20.329 --> 00:02:23.969
I think she's made a lot of money from, from
books and maybe speaking since, I'm not totally

00:02:23.969 --> 00:02:28.340
sure, but we've known that Elizabeth Warren
has a lot of money for a very long time.

00:02:28.340 --> 00:02:34.019
What I hate to break to people is that earning
$63,000 in extra income per year doing legal

00:02:34.019 --> 00:02:40.239
consulting when you are a relatively well
known and respected law professor is not shocking.

00:02:40.239 --> 00:02:45.859
It is not a crazy amount of money when we're
talking about Bloomberg and Trump and bayzos

00:02:45.859 --> 00:02:49.000
and, and you know, Sheldon Adelson and all
of this stuff.

00:02:49.000 --> 00:02:54.749
Elizabeth Warren over 30 years making 63 grand
a year doing legal work, which is what lawyers

00:02:54.749 --> 00:02:55.859
do.

00:02:55.859 --> 00:02:58.200
It's really not a scandal.

00:02:58.200 --> 00:03:04.659
Now, um, you can say some of the specific
people she represented are problematic.

00:03:04.659 --> 00:03:05.659
Okay.

00:03:05.659 --> 00:03:07.700
Now you've got a little bit better of an argument.

00:03:07.700 --> 00:03:13.389
She represented a company called LTV steel
or consulted for them who didn't want to pay

00:03:13.389 --> 00:03:15.749
into a fund for coal miners.

00:03:15.749 --> 00:03:17.470
She was on the wrong side of that.

00:03:17.470 --> 00:03:19.870
The progressive thing to do is you support
the miners.

00:03:19.870 --> 00:03:23.230
She was hired by LTV steel and she represented
them.

00:03:23.230 --> 00:03:24.510
Can we go after her for that?

00:03:24.510 --> 00:03:25.510
Sure.

00:03:25.510 --> 00:03:28.590
In the same way that you can go after a defense
attorney for representing someone that you

00:03:28.590 --> 00:03:30.590
think is guilty, that's fair game.

00:03:30.590 --> 00:03:33.480
That's just a question of what do we think
about lawyers?

00:03:33.480 --> 00:03:40.519
She advised Dow chemical about some breast
implant litigation and made 20 grand for that.

00:03:40.519 --> 00:03:44.709
It was Dow chemical on the side of people
who had been hurt by their breast implants.

00:03:44.709 --> 00:03:47.670
No, she wasn't, and we can criticize her for
that.

00:03:47.670 --> 00:03:49.639
She advised one of Enron's creditors.

00:03:49.639 --> 00:03:52.120
Remember Enron imploded and lots of people
lost money.

00:03:52.120 --> 00:03:54.279
She advised one event runs creditors.

00:03:54.279 --> 00:03:56.870
Most of the cases were pretty mundane and
they never made headlines.

00:03:56.870 --> 00:03:59.489
Now let's discuss the talking points that
are floating around.

00:03:59.489 --> 00:04:04.150
There are memes floating around about, wow,
a woman earns 2 million over 30 years.

00:04:04.150 --> 00:04:05.390
Oh my goodness.

00:04:05.390 --> 00:04:09.489
Meanwhile, Mike Bloomberg spends 35 million
in two weeks on his campaign and no one bats

00:04:09.489 --> 00:04:10.489
an eye.

00:04:10.489 --> 00:04:13.340
First of all, people are talking about how
much money Bloomberg is spending, so I don't

00:04:13.340 --> 00:04:17.109
think that it's fair to say there's not reporting
about that, but I don't think it's about male,

00:04:17.109 --> 00:04:18.489
female in particular here.

00:04:18.489 --> 00:04:20.530
I think it's about expectations.

00:04:20.530 --> 00:04:23.310
Bloomberg is held to a different standard.

00:04:23.310 --> 00:04:27.009
He is a billionaire buying his way into this
race.

00:04:27.009 --> 00:04:31.810
Elizabeth Warren is rightly seen as someone
closer to Bernie, but with a more corporate

00:04:31.810 --> 00:04:32.810
pass.

00:04:32.810 --> 00:04:33.810
There's no question.

00:04:33.810 --> 00:04:35.360
So I think this is the wrong area of focus.

00:04:35.360 --> 00:04:40.050
I don't think that this reveals anything new
about Elizabeth Warren.

00:04:40.050 --> 00:04:46.479
I am very concerned and have been about her
association with someone named Susie Orman

00:04:46.479 --> 00:04:52.620
who is a sort of financial pop finance person
who gives some kind of weird advice that's

00:04:52.620 --> 00:04:59.050
not new, but this entire 1.9 million earnings
over 30 years was pushed by the Buddha judge

00:04:59.050 --> 00:05:03.300
people and ultimately I don't think we've
really learned much from it on PR on policy.

00:05:03.300 --> 00:05:04.930
Bernie remains the most progressive.

00:05:04.930 --> 00:05:07.050
Elizabeth Warren is a close second.

00:05:07.050 --> 00:05:13.479
We know Bernie got to where he is politically
from a hippie activist past in Brooklyn and

00:05:13.479 --> 00:05:14.479
Vermont.

00:05:14.479 --> 00:05:18.449
Elizabeth Warren, on the other hand, has been
pulled left politically coming from a more

00:05:18.449 --> 00:05:21.419
centrist, status quo, legal, political, corporate
world.

00:05:21.419 --> 00:05:26.830
And, uh, we deal with their policy proposals
as they are today, period.

00:05:26.830 --> 00:05:30.060
And I don't think this is the right story
for the left to go crazy over.

00:05:30.060 --> 00:05:31.729
If I'm wrong, let me know.

00:05:31.729 --> 00:05:32.982
And no, I have not endorsed Elizabeth Warren
in this segment.

